<!-- ============================ ABOUT ============================ -->
<section id="about" class="section about" aria-labelledby="about-h">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="about-h">A school built by someone who spent 17 years studying them</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="founder">
      <figure class="portrait">
        <div class="portrait-frame" role="img" aria-label="Placeholder portrait of the founder"><span aria-hidden="true">HS</span></div>
        <figcaption><strong>Dr. Harshvardhan Shrivastva</strong>Founder and Principal. Portrait placeholder.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="story">
        <p>Dr. Harshvardhan Shrivastva holds a PhD in Education Policy from Harvard University. For 17 years in the United States he advised school districts, trained teachers and published research on one question: why do some schools lift every child while others quietly leave some behind?</p>
        <p>Every trip home to India showed him the other side of that question. He met bright children with real talent and no school that knew how to grow it. Understanding how great schools work felt incomplete if he never built one.</p>
        <p>So he came back. Endeavour International School in Bhopal is his answer: a school where classes are small enough for teachers to know every child, and where what research says about learning shapes the lessons children sit through each day.</p>
        <blockquote class="pull">
          What is the use of knowing how great schools work if I never build one for my own people?
          <footer>Dr. Harshvardhan Shrivastva, Founder and Principal</footer>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="vm">
      <div>
        <h3>Our vision</h3>
        <p>A school where every child is known, challenged and supported, and where talent from any home in Madhya Pradesh finds a place to grow.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Our mission</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Keep classes small so no child is overlooked.</li>
          <li>Teach in ways that research shows help children learn.</li>
          <li>Build confidence and character through clubs, sport and the arts.</li>
          <li>Work with parents as partners in each child's progress.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="why">
      <h3>Why parents choose Endeavour</h3>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Classes of 25 or fewer</dt><dd>Teachers can see who is quiet, who is racing ahead and who needs one more explanation.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>One teacher for every 15 students</dt><dd>Help is close at hand, in the classroom and outside it.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>A national board you can recognise</dt><dd>CISCE affiliation, with the ICSE examination at Class 10 and the ISC examination at Class 12.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>A principal who has studied schools for 17 years</dt><dd>Lesson planning and teacher training are shaped by his research and classroom work.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>A school day that works for families</dt><dd>8:00 AM to 2:30 PM, Monday to Saturday, with bus service across the city.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>More than exams</dt><dd>Debate, Model United Nations, coding, robotics and yoga are part of school life.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
